  "body": "What happens: the `freebsd` job of `release.yml` run 44164878190 (tag `v0.23.0`) fails. The first run and one re-run of the failed job stop at the same point.\n\n```\nCompiling boa_ast v0.21.1\nKilled\n##[error]ssh exited with code 137\n```\n\nThe result: the v0.23.0 release has 11 assets and no `camcraft-0.23.0-freebsd-amd64.tar.gz`. The v0.22.0 release has a FreeBSD package. The release notes on GitHub say that the FreeBSD build did not succeed.\n\nExpected: the job builds and uploads the FreeBSD package.\n\nEvidence:\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml`, job `freebsd`: `vmactions/freebsd-vm@v1` with `cpu: 3` and `mem: 5120`.\n- Exit code 137 is a kill signal. The probable cause is that the VM has no memory left during the compile. This is not confirmed.\n- All other jobs of the run are green (`publish` and `pages` included).\n\nPossible corrections (not decided):\n- Give the VM more memory, or build with fewer jobs (`cargo build -j 2`).\n- Add swap space in the VM before the build.\n\nOpen question: the workflow file of a tag run comes from the tag. A correction on `main` does not build the v0.23.0 package unless the workflow can build a given tag from `main`. The tag is not moved.\n\nWorkaround: build from source on FreeBSD.\n\nDone means: the `freebsd` job is green on a tag run, and the release has the FreeBSD package.\n",
